 5. Directive handling enters `src/orchestrator.rs::handle_agent_directives_streaming`.
 
+Selected-agent chat messages that start with a slash command and continue immediately with a
+non-whitespace command name use the provider-native backend command path instead of normal prompt
+stdin. For Codex sessions, `src/cli.rs::CommandChat::send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` detects that
+form and calls `src/agent_runtime.rs::AgentBackend::execute_command_streaming`; the Codex
+implementation builds `codex exec resume --json <thread-id> <command>` with empty stdin through
+`src/codex.rs::CodexBackend::build_command_invocation`. This keeps commands such as `/status` and
+`/fork` out of ordinary chat prompt wrapping while leaving non-command slash text on the normal
+message path.
+
 The process starts in `ReadPermission::Orchestrator` by default. The top-level
 `--no-read-permission` option selects `ReadPermission::DirectFilesystem`; in that mode the
 orchestrator no longer receives normal file-read requests from agents and cannot record those direct
